" cx=\"411.0496644295302\" cy=\"81.5167785234899\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(34%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Dhaka the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.47) and least in\n<b>winter</b> (-0.24).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>174</td><td class='num'>2%</td><td class='num'>-0.238</td><td class='num'>2.0%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>210</td><td class='num'>32%</td><td class='num'>-0.110</td><td class='num'>22.4%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>161</td><td class='num'>69%</td><td class='num'>0.008</td><td class='num'>19.1%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>171</td><td class='num'>37%</td><td class='num'>0.467</td><td class='num'>11.5%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":23.7104,"lon":90.40744,"n":716,"n_cities":213,"name":"Dhaka","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.18,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.017588652482269502,"n":282,"obs":0.01773049645390071,"sig":false},{"hi":0.53,"lo":0.18,"mean":0.34053333333333335,"n":75,"obs":0.12,"sig":true},{"hi":0.75,"lo":0